Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 21
Author: C. A. Wood
Date: 1927-09-17
Byline: Submitted by C. A. Wood, Syracuse, N. Y.
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-09-17_93/page/n31/mode/1up
Puzzle-Number: 21
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-09-24_93/page/n31/mode/1up


CORSET#LOANED
H#MULE#AMIR#E
AM#NAP#MAR#HP
SEA#NEVER#RUE
TALK#EEN#SIGN
ELBOWS#TIPPED
###RE###MO###
POTATO#SPONGE
ODIN#PET#LIRA
ION#BEERS#PAS
SR#AIR#OER#MT
O#EDDA#DEEP#E
NOOSES#EDITOR


A1. What is rarely ever known to hang around the girls? ~ CORSET
A6. What do snow shovels get in the Winter and lawn mowers in the Summer? ~ LOANED
A11. Name something that has a lot of kick. ~ MULE
A12. Who is a big gun in Afganistan? ~ AMIR
A13. What is the morning after the night before? (abbr.) ~ AM
A15. What is good for a rest? ~ NAP
A16. What did Gene Tunney do to Jack Dempsey the first time they met? ~ MAR
A17. What means of locomotion gets many an old bus out of a ditch? (abbr.) ~ HP
A18. What is wet even in the driest weather? ~ SEA
A20. When will America really become dry? ~ NEVER
A22. Name an herb of bitter taste and strong odor. ~ RUE
A23. What is the chief product of Washington, D. C.? ~ TALK
A25. What is "even" to the poet? ~ EEN
A26. What is the first thing sightseers see—and the last? ~ SIGN
A27. What joints are active in even dry countries? ~ ELBOWS
A29. What do "those who wait" usually want to be? ~ TIPPED
A31. Name a note in the musical scale. ~ RE
A32. What always comes on the first? (abbr.) ~ MO
A33. What has eyes but cannot see? ~ POTATO
A37. Name an ocean swell? ~ SPONGE
A41. Who was chief of the Teutonic Gods? ~ ODIN
A42. What is a favorite? ~ PET
A44. What is the equivalent of the franc in Italy? ~ LIRA
A45. What is the substance resulting from electrolytic decomposition? ~ ION
A46. What are known by the collars they wear? ~ BEERS
A48. What is a dance in France? ~ PAS
A49. What is an abbreviation for the old man? ~ SR
A50. What is the only free thing in the Land of the Free? ~ AIR
A51. What is usually over with the poet? ~ OER
A53. What is the Matterhorn? (abbr.) ~ MT
A54. Name a collection of Iceland tales. ~ EDDA
A55. Of what kind of stuff are philosophers made? ~ DEEP
A57. What was a necessary accessory of the old fashioned necking party? (Plural.) ~ NOOSES
A58. What kind of person is not noted for his taking ways? ~ EDITOR

D1. What people are always virtuous? ~ CHASTE
D2. What usually has a bath in the best hotels?(abbr.) ~ RM
D3. What is a regular setter? ~ SUN
D4. What did French troops attack with? ~ ELAN
D5. What is the home of the American Indian? (Plural) ~ TEPEES
D6. What do the bridegroom's friends do? ~ LAMENT
D7. Who was the anti-prohibitionist of Persia? ~ OMAR
D8. What does the breezy shiek often get? ~ AIR
D9. What kind of beer is ½ of 1% (abbr.) ~ NR
D10. What means "to be contingent?" ~ DEPEND
D14. What do prohibitionists get full on? ~ MEAL
D17. Name an adjective that fits an elephant. ~ HUGE
D19. What priestly vestment is worn at the Eucharist? ~ ALB
D21. Who was a brother of Odin? ~ VE
D22. What is a sad parting? ~ RIP
D24. What is a Shiek's Good Book? ~ KORAN
D26. What gets strung a lot? ~ SPOOL
D28. What was Rain-in-the-Face in a thunder storm? ~ WET
D30. What is a little devil? ~ IMP
D33. What did Lucretia Borgia serve for dessert? ~ POISON
D34. What does your nose know? ~ ODOR
D35. Where do sardines come from? ~ TIN
D36. Where are the High C's explored? ~ OPERAS
D37. How did Prince Carol travel the Primrose Path? ~ STRODE
D38. What is a small shot? ~ NIP
D39. What is the unit of weight in the metric system? ~ GRAM
D40. What day of the year affects most the heads of the ladies? ~ EASTER
D43. What is an abbreviation for elegant eels? ~ EE
D46. What would you have to do if you had a full house? ~ BIDE
D47. What does many an early bird catch? ~ SEED
D50. What do editors rarely ever reject? (abbr.) ~ ADS
D52. Name a Portuguese coin. ~ REI
D54. What is an abbreviation for elderly oryzoryctidae? ~ EO
D56. What did regular cowboys carry on the hip?(abbr.) ~ PT


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A12: Who is a big gun in Afganistan? → Afghanistan
D24: What is a Shiek's Good Book? → Sheik's
D8: What does the breezy shiek often get? → sheik

